he potential to be formidable  in the mortal kombat tournament a fact  that was also realized by the thunder  god  raiden and so seeing lou kang as the  best hope for earth realm  raiden takes him to train with beau  raicho a martial arts master who likes  to partake of alcoholic beverages and  employs a fighting style known as the  drunken  fist and so with all this training liu  kang earns the right to be one of the  warriors representing earth realm in the  mortal kombat tournament and raiden who  had become a mentor of luke hanks is  contacted by his future self and his  future self basically tells him  he must win now written believes that  the he that his future self is referring  to is luke hank because at that point  he's the only earthrealm warrior left in  the mortal kombat tournament so it just  made good sense now liu kang does win  the tournament after defeating goro and  shang tsung but when raiden's amulet  begins to crack  even more he starts to think that maybe  he'd misinterpreted the message he'd  received from his future self and that  maybe  luke hang was a loser and not a winner  now in the next mortal kombat tournament  raiden believes that kung lao a former  shaolin monk that's thought to be fairly  equal to liu kang in terms of ability  is the one that must win kung lao is  able to defeat both shang tsung and the  demonic sorcerer quan qi in a two-on-one  battle but just as it appears that kung  lao is on the brink of victory here  comes xiao khan who snaps his neck  earth  now because kung lao was basically liu  kang's bestie luke heng  isn't really happy about this he gets  mad as hell and he challenges shao khan  for killing his friend because you know  that's what you do when somebody kills  your friend now not only does he defeat  shao khan but it seems as if he kills  him although later it would be revealed  this was not the case and he actually  just mounts an invasion of earth realm  but the invasion is against the rules of  the mortal kombat tournament because  one realms only really permitted to  invade another if they best them in  mortal combat  10 consecutive times and at this point  luke hang had scored two consecutive  victories for  earth realm and so reign and liu kang go  to the elder gods who set up the rules  of the tournament in the first place to  try to convince them to intervene and  stop shao khan's invasion but despite  the invasion being a blatant violation  of the rules the elder gods are like no  we don't really care just uh  figure it out right we're watching  snowfall but following this raiden makes  a suggestion to ask quan chi for help  and luke kang just decides that raiden's  lost his mind and so raiden then reveals  that he now believes that the he  and he must win does not refer to liu  king or kung lao but to shao  and so liu kang challenges raiden but  raiden defeats him and then liu kang  hits raiden with his signature fiery  punch but when met with raiden's bolts  of electricity this backfires to  severely burn liu kang and then he  eventually dies from his injuries after  telling raiden  [Music]  you have killed us  now liu kang has then taken another  realm where he exists as an undead  revenant in service of quan chief and  after the elder god shinnok is freed liu  kang  pledges his allegiance to him and vows  to help him overthrow the other elder  gods because you know he's still pissed  off at raiden for killing him now liu  kang battles his former allies notably  raiden who once again  defeats him now once shinnok is defeated  luke king becomes one of the rulers of  the nether realm along with his  girlfriend katana and so liu kang  continues to be influenced by shinnok  and plans his own invasion of earth  realm the invasion is unsuccessful but  does lead to the return of  chronica a member of a race known as the  titans and the mother of shinnok you'd  think they'd get done  doing like family members of of shinnok  people like that and just be like here's  chronica  she taught him math in like the third  grade but chronica possesses the ability  to manipulate time and one result of  this is that the past version of liu  kang is brought to the present so now we  have a good luke hang and an evil loo  kang running around  the two versions of liu kang fight with  the younger version emerging victorious  the evil lou kang once again faces off  with raiden but only after raiden tries  to reason with him explaining that  chronica manipulated the timeline to  ensure that luke hang and raiden would  battle in every timeline and liu kang  was destined to die  every single time and so raiden defeats  lukang but instead of killing him he  merges himself with the revenant version  of liu kang as well as the physical body  of the deceased  liu kang creating fire god luke hank now  with his consciousness restored and in  possession of new godly powers  fire god luke kang is able to defeat an  entire army of chronica soldiers and  then battles chronicle herself who uses  her powers to take the battle  to the beginning of time but she's  eventually defeated by liu kang who uses  his fire abilities to turn her into  glass before destroying her which was  really really amazing but after this  luke hang and raiden are separated with  luke kang remaining a god while raiden  becomes mortal and so liu kang is given  the title of protector of earth realm  and keeper of time he then uses  chronica's hourglass to rewrite the  timeline itself which results in a  showdown between fire god luke hank and  shang tsung who's obtained kronika's  crown hoping to take on her role for  himself now how the battle plays out  depends on whether the player of the  game chooses to fight as shang tsung  or fire god liu kang and so i don't  really think we can really learn much  about the relative strength of either  based on this battle but the fact that  fire god luke hang was able to defeat  cronica who would probably be the  character that we're talking about here  if it weren't for the existence of fire  god liu kang is a testament to how  strong he really is  chronica was a threat that seemed  unbeatable until she wasn't as she was  able to affect the time stream itself  the fire god liu kang gets the job done  and literally saves the world and all of  creation from inevitable destruction but  because we see fire god liu kang for  such a short period of time we don't  really have any other feats to go on to  gauge his power level but liu kang was  honestly  extremely powerful already having  defeated some of the fiercest warriors  in mortal kombat including goro shang  tsung and xiao khan so when you take  probably the best fighter in the  entirety of the universe who already had  the ability to control fire in his  normal form and who given the powers of  the thunder god raiden which allows him  to become a firebender from the fire  nation this is pretty much  a no-brainer but with that being said  guys we're gonna bring this to an end  thank you all for watching and i will  catch you guys later  peace

